    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "edit.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add is_replace on impl Edit. Keep it public, the same way is_delete is public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is one condition: !self.old.is_empty() && !self.new.is_empty(). Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch is_insert or is_delete. The existing test an_insert_has_no_old_text stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_replacement_has_old_and_new_text checks an edit with old a and new b is true. Edit::insert of ab is false. Edit::delete of ab is false. An edit with both strings empty is false. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
